ld talk  to you someone that's experienced in  that does it for a profession that lives  in that world and so I'm not saying I'm  the brain surgeon of Saudi Arabia but  there I have experience to talk to those  that have experience do your research on  your own check out different videos and  come up with your own conclusions and I  can only speak from my experience there  which was overall excellent I had two  weeks there it was a big eye-opener I  learned a ton Wow it was it was one of  the coolest trips I've ever taken so  here's some practical advice for you  I'll just take deal with the basics here  first visas super easy online took me  like ten minutes  I think I got the visa that day in my  email you print it off and when you  check through immigrations easy breeze  no problems they're out of the airport  uber took a goober into my hotel in  Riyadh hotels there look the country is  not set up for tourism it hasn't had  many tourists so there are many business  travels there many expats or foreigners  living there but as far as being a  traveler well there are a lot of  travelers from Mecca and Medina and the  religious sites but say being a Western  traveler who is not allowed to go until  just recently  well hotels $50 will get you something  pretty good not great fifty sixty  dollars on the budget front you can do  couchsurfing they do do couchsurfing  that's free so if you want to go super  cheap that's the way to go but as far as  like backpacker hostels I think that  sure will develop there's not so much of  it now and then you can get all the real  expensive hotels if you want  infrastructures good in the country so  getting around on the highways or flying  is excellent and you do have to do those  things it's a big country look at a map  and see like you know measure it on  Google with your fingers and then  compare it to where you're from and see  the distances because Riyadh to Jeddah  is quite a ways  I think I'm roughly eight or nine hour  drive 