ve everything from woman covering full  covers as you'd imagine to woman with no  cover and that is something I didn't  know about and that is something that is  really I'd say overexposed in the West  that whole topic as in most women and  Saudi are prisoners and they're all kept  under cover and super complicated it's a  complicated country I met a woman in a  niqab that chooses to wear it and it's  not because of her family it's not  because of her religious because she  wants to and then I'm sure there are  women that don't want to and then there  there's everything and so again it's  been overexposed in Western media and I  feel a little bit silly honestly at this  point how little I knew about this and  actually how little I knew about Saudi I  think Saudi is one of the most actually  I think it's the most misunderstood  country in the world  I used to say Iran was because I've  gotten Iran a couple times I think Saudi  is the winner now is the most  misunderstood I was a little bit nervous  flying in I'm you know I was like do  they all hate Westerners do they you  know as is it gonna be like super closed  off and I thought it would be because of  well tourism was just opened up recently  but it wasn't  like people are super hospitable like  over-the-top hospitable invite you into  their homes invite you to eat with them  give you presents so it's a country that  in that respect is super easy to travel  and like I showed up at some guy's house  randomly walked up he invited me in gave  me this what I found out later was some  very expensive honey and this is the  treatment I received all over the  country so if you like a culture if you  want to connect with the place if you go  in with an open mind and an open heart  the people will open up fully a very  cool component to it okay what else do I  got here English in the cities the  Saudis speak English quite well that was  surprising I'm in Spain now they speak  way better English and Saudi than Spain  clothe